### catalogue-choice-draw-e2e.http
###
### kanban/in-progress/catalogue-choice-draws-plan.md WI-9 — checked-in record of
### the end-to-end verification run against a live API + real PostgreSQL, per
### the plan's own precedent (bind-parameter-e2e.http's WI-8) of not leaving
### an undocumented manual e2e step.
###
### This file was executed for real on 2026-08-16 against:
###   - a throwaway Postgres 16 container (docker run postgres:16-alpine)
###   - `dotnet run --project src/Soarscore.Api --urls http://localhost:5299`
### and every response below matches what the run actually returned. It is
### also intended to be re-run as a regression check: start the two processes
### above, open this file in Rider's HTTP Client, and run top to bottom.
###
### A companion body file sits next to this one — `publish-f3k-body.json` —
### wrapping the real seed definition (tools/Soarscore.SeedData/json/10-f3k.json)
### in the `{"definition": {...}}` envelope `PublishClassDefinition` actually
### requires, the same convention `publish-f5k-body.json` (already checked in
### by bind-parameter-e2e.http) already follows. If either seed file changes,
### regenerate its wrapped copy here.
###
### THIS FILE COMPLETES bind-parameter-e2e.http's ABANDONED F5K LEG. That
### file's own header records: "Both of F5K's phases are ChooseFromCatalogue
### ... which trips drawPhase.unsupportedRoundComposition ... before the
### parameter-binding check is ever reached ... Binding minPerGroup here
### would not change this outcome." Catalogue-choice draws are now
### implemented, and the real run below shows F5K reaching
### drawPhase.parameterUnbound for the first time, exactly as bind-parameter's
### plan originally predicted before the catalogue-choice gap was discovered.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5299

### =====================================================================
### Part 1 — F3K: a catalogue draw naming five distinct tasks succeeds.
### =====================================================================

### 1. Publish F3K's real class definition.
### Actual response in this run: 200, body
###   "f049fcea21944528de98792dda60e9b7152d32380f06f7e93306c6775b612098"
POST {{baseUrl}}/publish-class-definition
Content-Type: application/json

< ./publish-f3k-body.json

> {%
    client.global.set("f3kHash", JSON.parse(response.body));
%}

### 2. Create a competition adopting F3K.
### Actual response: 200, body {"value":"01a00920-ae4f-7967-b9da-c9919aaed71d"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/create-competition
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "F3K E2E Test",
  "location": "Taupo",
  "startDate": "2026-01-10",
  "endDate": "2026-01-12",
  "classContentHash": "{{f3kHash}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("f3kCompId", JSON.parse(response.body).value);
%}

### 3. Register six people + competitors — enough for F3K's literal
### MinPerGroup of 5 (task A and every task that inherits its Group via
### `with`). Run 1..6, reusing the same "f3kPersonId" variable per pair,
### the same convention bind-parameter-e2e.http's NZ-M block uses.
###
### Pilot 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/register-person
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Pilot F3K 1", "contact": { "email": "pilot-f3k-1@example.com" }, "club": null }

> {% client.global.set("f3kPersonId", JSON.parse(response.body).value); %}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/register-competitor
Content-Type: application/json

{ "competitionId": { "value": "{{f3kCompId}}" }, "personId": { "value": "{{f3kPersonId}}" } }

